== a bash shebang selects the bash mood:
bash
== an sh shebang selects the posix mood:
sh
== an env shebang selects the named shell:
sh
== a script with no shebang keeps the session mood:
kosh
== the shebang is unread without -I:
kosh
== an explicit --mood wins:
kosh
== --dumb wins:
sh
== an sh invocation name wins:
sh
== the mimicked mood relaxes the strict options:
[]
rc=0
== an explicit -u stays fatal:
TMPDIR/unset-script:2:8: error: Unable to expand 'undefined_name' because the parameter is not set.
     2 |  echo "[${undefined_name}]"
       |         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Replace it with ${undefined_name-} if empty expansion is desired.
rc=1
== the strict default still reports the unset read:
TMPDIR/unset-script:2:8: error: The variable 'undefined_name' is read before any assignment gives it a value. (SC2154)
     2 |  echo "[${undefined_name}]"
       |         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Assign 'undefined_name' before it is read, or set it in the environment.
rc=1
